From: GitHub Copilot <copilot@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] contrib: disable harfbuzz utilities (Apple meson cross file lacks objcpp)

HarfBuzz 14.x util/ requires an 'objcpp' binary in the meson cross file on
Darwin, which VLC's generated cross file does not define, failing the Apple
contrib build (harfbuzz/util/meson.build: 'objcpp' compiler binary not
defined). The utilities are CLI tools libvlc never links; disable them so
only the library (incl. coretext shaping) is built.
---
--- a/contrib/src/harfbuzz/rules.mak
+++ b/contrib/src/harfbuzz/rules.mak
@@ -25,7 +25,8 @@ HARFBUZZ_CONF := -Dfreetype=enabled \
 	-Dgobject=disabled \
 	-Ddocs=disabled \
 	-Dtests=disabled \
-	-Dgpu_demo=disabled
+	-Dgpu_demo=disabled \
+	-Dutilities=disabled
 
 ifdef HAVE_DARWIN_OS
 HARFBUZZ_CONF += -Dcoretext=enabled
